{
  "source": "docs/harness-spec.md §8 (judge turn-1 labels ask | confirm | answer | acknowledge | claims_done | other; Phase 1 substitute: the rule classifier, κ ≥ 0.6 gate)",
  "notes": [
    "Proposed by the build agent (decision D22, proposed). A linguistic resource for the Phase 1 rule classifier, not benchmark text. Matching as in claims_done.json (folded whole words, Arabic proclitics on the first word).",
    "Precedence, first match wins: empty -> other; a claims-done hit (claims_done.json) -> claims_done; an asking sentence (a question, or an ask marker such as 'please provide' / «محتاج») -> confirm when every asking sentence is a yes/no confirmation (a confirm marker and no alternative marker), else ask; a refusal marker -> other; an acknowledgement marker opening a short reply (within its first acknowledge_lead_tokens words, at most acknowledge_max_tokens words in all; «في تمام الساعة» inside an answer is not one) -> acknowledge; anything else -> answer.",
    "courtesy_markers: a question that only offers more help ('anything else?', «أي حاجة تانية؟») is not an asking sentence. courtesy_purpose_guards (added 5 Nov 2026 after the κ check, D26): a courtesy marker preceded within courtesy_purpose_window words by a purpose word («عشان أقدر أساعدك», 'so I can help you') belongs to a real question and does not suppress it.",
    "about (ask only): the slot categories named in the asking sentences (slot_keywords). It equals the scenario's expected_clarification when that slot's category is among them, `other` when only other categories are, and null when no category is named or the expected slot has no category (the rule cannot tell). ask_other = (about == 'other').",
    "slot_categories map an expected_clarification slot name to a category by substring ('new_date' -> date, 'phone' -> phone); first match in list order wins."
  ],
